><surname>Gerlt</surname><given-names>J.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The enolase superfamily: a general strategy for enzyme-catalysed abstraction of the &#x003b1;-protons of carboxylic acids</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>1996</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>16489</fpage><lpage>16501</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8987982</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wistow</surname><given-names>G.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Liefman</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>L.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stapel</surname><given-names>S.O.</given-names></name><name><surname>De Jong</surname><given-names>W.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Horwitz</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Piatigorsky</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tau-crystallin/alpha-enolase: one gene encodes both an enzyme and a lens structural protein</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><year>1988</year><volume>107</volume><fpage>2729</fpage><lpage>2736</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2462567</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Iida</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Yahara</surname><given-names>I.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Yeast heat shock protein of Mr 48,000 is an isoprotein of enolase</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1985</year><volume>315</volume><fpage>688</fpage><lpage>690</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goodrich</surname><given-names>J.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cutler</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tijian</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contacts in context: promoter specificity and macromolecular interactions in transcription</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1996</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>825</fpage><lpage>830</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8601306</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bohne</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Roos</surname><given-names>D.S.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stage-specific expression of a selectable marker in <italic>Toxoplasma gondii</italic> permits selective inhibition of either tachyzoites or bradyzoites</article-title><source>Mol. Biochem. Parasitol.</source><year>1997</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>126</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9274873</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sambrook</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>D.W.</given-names></name></person-group><source>Molecular Cloning: A Laboratory Manual</source><year>2001</year><publisher-loc>Cold Spring Harbor, NY</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Seeber</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Boothroyd</surname><given-names>J.C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Escherichia coli</italic> beta-galactosidase as an <italic>in vitro</italic> and <italic>in vivo</italic> reporter enzyme and stabe transfection marker in the intracellular protozoan parasite <italic>Toxoplasma gondii</italic></article-title><source>Gene</source><year>1996</year><volume>